Exactly one SUCCESS, same random delay as Exp2. The "entering/leaving
critical section" pairs show Worker-2 and Worker-3 both received their
requests early (#4, #5) but could not enter the critical section until
Worker-1 finished and unlocked (#7) — the mutex serializes the
check-then-write sequence, so every worker that arrives after the first
one always sees the up-to-date RESERVED state instead of a stale
AVAILABLE one. This is the fix for the race condition shown in exp2.log.
